      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The most significant weakness in the UBI argument is the sheer, unsustainable cost, which necessitates massive tax hikes or crippling national debt. Opponents will hammer the inflationary risk, arguing that injecting universal cash without corresponding productivity increases will simply drive up the cost of living, negating the benefit. Your student must counter by asserting that the cost is an investment in human capital, which ultimately drives economic growth and reduces the massive hidden costs of poverty and bureaucracy.",
