    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the cost/inflation stuff is a good start, but that feels a bit like standard textbook stuff. i need them to win. give me some more aggressive, deep-cut rebuttals that really undermine the moral foundation of the UBI argument. like, what are the most damning ways to argue that UBI is actually harmful to society or the individual? i need the kind of points that make the pro side look delusional.",
