      "content": "The moral foundation of UBI is dangerously naive because it fundamentally devalues the necessity of work, promoting societal dependency rather than self-reliance. A truly robust society values contribution, and decoupling income from effort sends a corrosive message that basic survival is a right independent of personal responsibility. Furthermore, UBI risks creating a permanent underclass reliant on government handouts, eroding the vital civic virtue of striving and ambition.",
      "source": "target",
